Z||000000||GT Bastard||03-23-2000||09:03 PM||||After much consideration, I've decided to go through with the auto to manual swap.  I'm going to start buying parts in the next few days (tranny, clutch, shift cables, etc...)<P>I leaning towards the 4sp Muncie with 4.10 final drive ratio, but the local Salvage yard here has a couple Getrag 5sp trannies from a Fiero for 150 bucks each...  So far I've found the Muncie's for 125, but I've only called one yard so far. <P>1) Is there a casting # on the tranny that will allow me to distinguish between gear ratio's on both trannies?<P>2) If I decide to rebuild it first, can the tranny be built more durably?<P>3) What are your thoughts on the 4sp Muncie and 5sp Getrag???  <P>4) What type of clutch would you guys recommend?  Maybe a RAM?<P>At the same time we do the tranny swap, my father and I are going to install a compucam and a chip.<P>Thanks in advance for your help!<P>-The Bastard||||reg||1
