Z||000006||SCCA FIERO||03-24-2000||10:10 PM||||1) I think 86.5-87 Getrags are the same and 88's have a slightly lower FD, but I am not sure.<P>2) Dunno....sorry<P>3) Both are strong and durable, but the 4 speeds are inferior to the Getrags as far as clutch pedal stiffness and actual shifting (in my experiences anyway)<P>4)Not sure about this one... never had one.<P>Where do you live? If those trannys are Getrags and the shaft will move freely by turning it by hand and you can shift the levers pretty easily I may be interested in them(or the one you don't want). Are you sure these are Getrags? Fiero Getrags? I have one already and always looking for more.||||reg||1
Z||000007||pherder||03-24-2000||10:57 PM||||Here is a post from the Fiero list:<P>Hope this helps.<P>Paul<P>Scott A. Backer wrote:<P>&gt; &gt;   YEAR ---1984---   ---1985---   ---1986---   1987--1988<BR>&gt; &gt;  Model  Std  econ   4cyl  6cyl   4cyl  6cyl   4cyl  6cyl<BR>&gt; &gt;        ----  ----   ----  ----   ----  ----   ----  ----<BR>&gt; &gt; Final  3.32  2.42   3.35  3.65   3.35  3.65   3.35  3.65<BR>&gt; &gt;   1st  3.53  3.53   3.73  3.31   3.73  3.31   3.73  3.50<BR>&gt; &gt;   2nd  1.95  1.95   2.04  1.95   2.04  1.95   2.04  2.05<BR>&gt; &gt;   3rd  1.24  1.24   1.45  1.24   1.45  1.24   1.45  1.38<BR>&gt; &gt;   4th  0.81  0.81   1.03  0.81   1.03  0.81   1.03  0.94<BR>&gt; &gt;   5th  ----  ----   0.74  ----   0.74  ----   0.74  0.72<BR>&gt; &gt;   rev  3.42  3.42   3.50  3.42   3.50  3.42   3.50  3.41<BR>&gt;<BR>&gt; I have never seen a 1984 4-speed with a 2.42 final drive ratio and cannot find a RPO code listed for it. Also the 0.81 forth gear ratio was only used on the M17 4-speed used with the V6 in 1985,86.<BR>&gt;<BR>&gt;                                                  Final<BR>&gt;          RPO    1st    2nd    3rd    4th   5th   Drive<BR>&gt; 1984 L4  MY8   3.53   1.95   1.24   0.73         3.32<BR>&gt;               11.72   6.47   4.12   2.42<BR>&gt;<BR>&gt; 1984 L4  M19   3.53   1.95   1.24   0.73         4.10<BR>&gt;               14.47   8.00   5.08   2.99<BR>&gt;<BR>&gt; 1985 L4  MT2   3.73   2.04   1.45   1.03  0.74   3.35<BR>&gt;               12.50   6.83   4.86   3.45  2.48<BR>&gt;<BR>&gt; 1985 V6  M17   3.31   1.95   1.24   0.81         3.65<BR>&gt;               12.08   7.12   4.53   2.96<BR>&gt;<BR>&gt; 1986 L4  MT2   3.73   2.04   1.45   1.03  0.74   3.35<BR>&gt;               12.50   6.83   4.86   3.45  2.48<BR>&gt;<BR>&gt; 1986 V6  M17   3.31   1.95   1.24   0.81         3.65<BR>&gt;               12.08   7.12   4.53   2.96<BR>&gt;<BR>&gt; 1987 L4  MT2   3.73   2.04   1.45   1.03  0.74   3.35<BR>&gt;               12.50   6.83   4.86   3.45  2.48<BR>&gt;<BR>&gt; 1987 V6  MG2   3.50   2.05   1.38   0.94  0.72   3.61<BR>&gt;               12.64   7.40   4.98   3.39  2.60<BR>&gt;<BR>&gt; 1988 L4  MT2   3.73   2.04   1.45   1.03  0.74   3.35<BR>&gt;               12.50   6.83   4.86   3.45  2.48<BR>&gt;<BR>&gt; 1988 V6  MG2   3.50   2.05   1.38   0.94  0.72   3.61<BR>&gt;               12.64   7.40   4.98   3.39  2.60<BR>&gt;<BR>&gt; Scott A. Backer<BR>&gt; 106 Walnut Street<BR>&gt; Penn Yan, NY 14527-1329<BR>&gt; 315-536-0432<BR>&gt; sbacker@linkny.com<P>||||reg||1
